messages:
maya: Opening a docs PR to consolidate structured-output and tool-calling examples into one canonical page (node + python snippets) and a short migration checklist. PR: https://git.redwood/docs/pull/520

alex: Good. Which old snippets are we keeping vs removing? We have a bunch of tiny variants that confuse readers.

samantha: I can take the guardrails section and make it prescriptive: validation, explicit action enums, and a schema-version field. Short bullets, no heavy prose.

maya: Plan: keep the minimal canonical shapes that match the SDK samples. Deprecate the "array-wrapper" and the older multi-envelope variants; add an archived_examples.md with brief rationale.

kevin: For parsing patterns, let's recommend: strict JSON schema as primary; then a tiny fallback that attempts JSON.parse and falls back to a deterministic heuristic. That covers most real integrations.

maya: Suggested schema in the doc (small):
```json
{
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "cmd": { "type": "string" },
    "params": { "type": "array", "items": {"type":"string"} },
    "schema_version": { "type": "string" }
  },
  "required": ["cmd", "schema_version"]
}
```

maya: And the fallback helper we want in SDK snippets (node):
```js
function parseWithFallback(text) {
  try {
    return JSON.parse(text);
  } catch (e) {
    const m = /cmd:\s*(\w+)/i.exec(text);
    return { cmd: m ? m[1] : 'unknown', raw: text };
  }
}
module.exports = { parseWithFallback };
```

erin: Heads-up 12 our current node SDK returns the raw string when output isn't JSON. We'll add the helper and export it; I opened a small SDK PR: https://git.redwood/sdk/pulls/48

alex: I'll review that SDK PR today. If we standardize on `parseWithFallback` we should reference it from the docs snippets so readers can copy/paste.

samantha: Guardrails draft: (1) validate required fields and version, (2) enumerate allowed cmd values, (3) keep payloads shallow and typed. Also add a quick note about including an example raw string in tests so fallback paths get exercised.

kevin: I'll add a tiny docs CI check: run the node helper against all examples; fail the PR if any canonical example doesn't parse (either directly or via the fallback). Will attach the job to the PR.

maya: Also cleaning links 10 external-friendly versions. Replace internal.redwood/* links with /docs/ or public equivalents before merge.

docs-bot: preview: https://deploy-preview.redwood.dev/parse-canonical

samantha: Preview looks fine. Two copy nits: change "accepts a single string" -> "accepts a plain string body" and tighten the example response for readability.

erin: I kicked off the docs link-checker on the branch; it flagged two internal-only URLs and one bad relative path.

maya: Fixed the bad paths and swapped internal links. Pushed updates to the PR branch.

alex: SDK PR LGTM, left a small comment about JSDoc for the helper. Will merge once CI is green.

kevin: Added the docs CI job and a test harness. It will run parseWithFallback against each example file. If parsing returns an object with schema_version missing, it fails.

maya: Great. Merge plan: wait for sdk/pulls/48 to merge, then merge this docs PR after link-check & docs CI pass. I'll add a short migration note and changelog line before merge.

maya: (edited) closing loop: archive old examples, publish canonical page, and notify customers via changelog.
